depthai-core v3.10.0: keep the device firmware out of RAM once booted.

Applied by the depthai stage of Dockerfile. Upstream:
- dai::initialize() unpacks the whole firmware archives on a background
  thread and keeps them for the life of the process (main firmware,
  4 OpenVINO patches, 2 bootloaders: ~88 MB);
- ArchiveUtil::readEntry() grows each file's buffer to twice its size
  (zero-filled, so touched) for its final, empty read;
- every boot copies the 38 MB firmware into the XLinkConnection, which
  keeps it as long as the device stays connected.
With this patch the firmware is unpacked only while a device boots,
into one exactly sized buffer, moved into the connection and dropped
after the boot (a reconnect builds a new connection and unpacks it
again). Measured with gateway/cpp/tools/depthai_probe.cpp.

